From: OpenIRD contributors
Subject: [PATCH] mips: delay: spell the HI-register multiply in C so modern gcc builds it

GCC dropped the MIPS "h" (HI register) asm constraint after 4.3, so this
tree does not build with the pinned gcc 4.9.4: every file that reaches
udelay() fails with

  include/asm/delay.h:81:3: error: impossible constraint in 'asm'
     __asm__("multu\t%2, %3"

The asm computes the high word of the 32x32 product.  Say that in C and
let the compiler choose the instruction -- it still emits multu/mfhi, so
the arithmetic and therefore the delay are unchanged.  Only the 32-bit
branch is touched; the 64-bit ones are dead code on this SoC
(CONFIG_32BIT=y) and are left alone.

Upstream fixed this differently, by moving __udelay out of line into
arch/mips/lib/delay.c (v2.6.33 era), which also changed the scaling
constant.  We keep this tree's constant so the timing stays exactly what
the vendor kernel had.

Origin: gpl-derived
---
--- a/include/asm-mips/delay.h
+++ b/include/asm-mips/delay.h
@@ -77,12 +77,18 @@
 	                           0x80000000ULL) >> 32);
 #endif
 
-	if (sizeof(long) == 4)
-		__asm__("multu\t%2, %3"
-		: "=h" (usecs), "=l" (lo)
-		: "r" (usecs), "r" (lpj)
-		: GCC_REG_ACCUM);
-	else if (sizeof(long) == 8 && !R4000_WAR)
+	if (sizeof(long) == 4) {
+		/*
+		 * The high word of the 32x32 product -- exactly what the
+		 * "multu + =h" asm produced.  Spelled in C because gcc
+		 * dropped the MIPS "h" (HI register) constraint after 4.3;
+		 * the compiler still emits multu/mfhi here.
+		 */
+		unsigned long long prod;
+
+		prod = (unsigned long long) usecs * (unsigned long long) lpj;
+		usecs = (unsigned long) (prod >> 32);
+	} else if (sizeof(long) == 8 && !R4000_WAR)
 		__asm__("dmultu\t%2, %3"
 		: "=h" (usecs), "=l" (lo)
 		: "r" (usecs), "r" (lpj)
